===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# An [[Irish#Adjective|Irish]] [[form#Noun|form]] of [[football#Noun|football]] [[play#Verb|played]] by [[two]] [[team#Noun|teams]] of 15 [[player]]s each, who [[score#Verb|score]] by [[kick#Verb|kicking]] or [[punch#Verb|punching]] a [[ball#Noun|ball]] into the [[opposing#Adjective|opposing]] team's [[goal#Noun|goal]] or over a [[crossbar]] and between two [[upright#Adjective|upright]] [[post#Noun|posts]] above the goals.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Brian Cosgrove|chapter=Sport, Politics and the ‘Other Side’|title=The Yew Tree at the Head of the Strand|location=Liverpool|publisher={{w|Liverpool University Press}}|year=2001|pages=143–144|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=etTS-AjV2RkC&pg=PA144|isbn=978-0-85323-737-2|passage=Armagh (and it is one of the most memorable chapters in the history of '''Gaelic football''') were fated to fall at the final hurdle when they were beaten by Kerry in the All-Ireland decider.}}

